  "versionIdentifier": "1998",
  "versionSpecification": "The 1998 version was constructed using a two-stage linear registration and averaging procedure (Holmes et al., 1998). In the first stage, each T1-weighted MRI volume was registered to stereotaxic space using an automated volumetric registration procedure (MRITOTAL) and resampled onto a 1 mm isotropic voxel grid. The registered volumes were averaged to generate an initial anatomical reference, which was subsequently used as the registration target for a second alignment of the original acquisitions. This refinement reduced residual registration variability and anatomical blurring, while repeated-image averaging improved the signal-to-noise ratio (SNR) and anatomical definition. The resulting anatomical average was linearly aligned with the MNI305 stereotaxic reference. The distributed dataset includes the averaged T1-weighted volume and accompanying brain and head masks."
